*  m1_defer_ALT.sno -- FINDING-2026-08-17-s139 sec.2 table, row 1 (defer_ALT).
*
*  ARBNO body defers to *Command; Command's tail is an UNDEFERRED alternation
*  Sp = SPAN(' ') | LEN(0).  Isolates "ALT reachable through an ARBNO-body
*  defer" from beauty's larger shape (m1_beauty_arbno_defer_min.sno).
*  Oracle (SPITBOL x64 sbl -b): ok.  scrip HEAD @ s139: FAIL.
*  Sibling set -- change exactly ONE ingredient at a time:
*    m1_defer_SPAN  -- Sp loses the LEN(0) alternate (no ALT at all)
*    m1_defer_LEN0  -- Sp loses the SPAN alternate (no ALT, no carve)
*    m1_inline_ALT  -- the alternation moves inline, no separate defer
*    m1_nodefer_ALT -- Command uses Sp directly, not *Sp (no defer at all)
         &ANCHOR      =  1
         Word         =  SPAN('ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ')
         Sp           =  SPAN(' ') | LEN(0)
         Command      =  Word *Sp
         L            =  ARBNO(*Command)
         Src          =  'START HERE'
         Src          POS(0) L RPOS(0)                            :F(FA)
         OUTPUT       =  'ok'                                     :(END)
FA       OUTPUT       =  'FAIL'
END
